# Design tokens for color

The **`tokens` object** in [src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) is the source of truth for the MIT Sailing marketing palette.

- **Foreground text:** use **`tokens.colors.text`** (`#2D2D2D`) for all readable copy—including labels, secondary lines, and captions. For visual hierarchy, use **font size, weight, or spacing**, not a lower-contrast gray without verified contrast.
- Do not use raw `#2D2D2D`, `#000000`, or `rgb(45, 45, 45)` when **`tokens.colors.text`** applies—use the token so values stay aligned.
- **Brand reds / surfaces / borders:** use **`tokens.colors.mitRed`**, **`mitRedHover`**, **`mitRedHighlight`**, **`surface`**, **`border`**, etc.—not one-off hexes.
- **New roles:** add a named entry under `tokens.colors` instead of scattering new hex values in JSX.

**Focus rings / Tailwind arbitrary colors:** If a class needs the same chroma as primary text, keep the value in sync with **`tokens.colors.text`** (see `textFocusRingClassName` in the same file) or refactor so the hex is not duplicated.

**Authentication UI:** Login, signup, forgot/reset password, verify/unlock flows, and `src/components/auth/*` must use MIT theme utilities (see [mit-auth-ui-colors.mdc](mit-auth-ui-colors.mdc)) — not **`blue-*`** utilities or arbitrary MIT red hex literals.
